[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605201900-etzhayyim-kuni-umi-s5-extended-sovereignty", :adr/title "ADR-2605201900: kuni-umi S5 — extended sovereignty deployment (S5a river / S5b ocean / S5c atmosphere / S5d orbit; stewardship-only operation; 4 new robot classes; final roadmap phase)", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605201900: kuni-umi S5 — Extended Sovereignty Deployment\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-05-20\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n# Context\n\nS1-S4 は all terrestrial — LandRegistry 4-layer substrate (Base L2 NFT + geth-private + IPFS GeoJSON + LANDS.md) の範囲内で religious-corp が utility 施工を進める pattern を確立。\n\nADR-2605192330 (Extended Land Sovereignty) は terrestrial を越える **4 domain** に extended sovereignty doctrine を proposed したが、その時点では doctrinal stance であり物理 deployment actor を持っていなかった:\n\n| Domain | International framework | Sovereignty pattern |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Ocean** | UNCLOS (海洋法条約) — EEZ / territorial water / 公海 | 沿岸国 sovereignty + 国際公域 — religious-corp は stewardship-only claim |\n| **River** | 水利権 (日本国内 — 河川法 + 水利使用許可) | 国 / 都道府県 / 流域 — religious-corp は dual-recognition pattern |\n| **Atmosphere** | Chicago Convention (国際民間航空条約) + 各国 airspace 主権 | 国家 airspace sovereignty + ICAO standards — religious-corp は HAPS / high-altitude platform で stewardship-only |\n| **Orbit** | Outer Space Treaty (宇宙条約 1967) + ITU 周波数 + COPUOS | 国家責任 + non-appropriation principle — religious-corp は registered launching state (Japan / others) 経由で stewardship 主張 |\n\nS5 で kuni-umi はこの 4 domain で physical infrastructure deployment を初めて実行する。**重要 invariant**: religious-corp は **operational sovereignty を主張しない** (ADR-2605192245 §6 + ADR-2605192330 §3 dual-recognition stance を physical layer で堅持)。\n\n## Constitutional gating\n\nS5 規模 + multi-domain は per-domain constitutional gate に加え **extended sovereignty governance vote** (ADR-2605192330 §4) を全 sub-stage で必須:\n\n| Sub-stage | Domain | Gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| S5a | River | 50% quorum + 2/3 supermajority (Extended Sovereignty) + per-prefecture 水利使用許可 |\n| S5b | Ocean | 50% quorum + 2/3 supermajority + UNCLOS coastal state coordination |\n| S5c | Atmosphere | 50% quorum + 2/3 supermajority + Chicago Conv. signatory state liaison + ICAO standards compliance |\n| S5d | Orbit | 50% quorum + 2/3 supermajority + registered launching state (e.g., Japan/JAXA) responsibility chain + ITU spectrum coordination + COPUOS notification |\n\n# Decision\n\n## 1. Sub-stage sequencing (S5a → S5d)\n\nS5 は **4 sub-stage に明示的に分割**、それぞれ独立 deployment + acceptance + Council Lv6+ supermajority gate。順序は **international complexity ascending**:\n\n| Order | Sub-stage | Domain | Rationale for ordering |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **S5a** | River | 日本国内 法務範囲 (河川法 + 水利使用許可) で international treaty 直接介在なし — kuni-umi が international domain 経験を積む onramp |\n| 2 | **S5b** | Ocean (coastal / EEZ inner) | UNCLOS coastal state + 漁業権 conflicts; territorial water (12 海里) 内に scope 限定 |\n| 3 | **S5c** | Atmosphere (HAPS) | Chicago Conv. 上 ICAO standards + 国土交通省 認可; stratosphere 18-25 km tethered platform に scope 限定 |\n| 4 | **S5d** | Orbit (LEO microsat) | Outer Space Treaty + 宇宙活動法 + ITU + JAXA registered launching state coordination; 最大複雑性 + 最大コスト |\n\n各 sub-stage は **完全独立 ADR + 完全独立 governance vote**。本 ADR は S5 全体 scope + 各 sub-stage gate を establish、specific deployment ADR は sub-stage 毎に別途。\n\n## 2. Stewardship-only operational invariant (CRITICAL)\n\nS5 全 4 domain で religious-corp は次の operational invariant を堅持:\n\n> **kuni-umi MUST NOT assert operational sovereignty in any extended-sovereignty domain.** Religious-corp が deploy する physical asset (river micro-hydro / coastal aquaculture / HAPS / orbital satellite) は **steward が運用** し、国際法上の sovereign authority (沿岸国 / airspace state / 登録 launching state / spectrum 主管) との **dual-recognition pattern** で coexist する。Religious-corp は asset owner ではなく asset steward。\n\nImplementation:\n\n- 全 S5 asset DID は path-based DID `did:web:etzhayyim.com:kuniumi:s5:<domain>:<assetCode>`、ownership field を **持たない** (vs terrestrial S1-S4 では stewardDid + landOwnerDid の 2 field)\n- 各 asset record には `internationalLawAttestationCid` (IPFS) を必須 field として持ち、Council Lv6+ Seat 3 (Legal-Ethics) が per-domain attestation を発行\n- Asset の operational decision (e.g., orbital satellite の station-keeping burn, HAPS の altitude profile) は **registered launching state / sovereign state** の jurisdiction; religious-corp は telemetry observer + steward coordinator のみ\n- 国際 conflict 時 (e.g., 別国家が asset を claim) 国際法上 sovereign state に notification + ICJ proceeding を国家経由で進めるパターン (religious-corp は non-state でも protected interest claim 可能、ただし sovereign state authority に最終 deferral)\n\nこれは ADR-2605192100 §mission.parallel_governance_to_state を physical deployment に拡張する constitutional commitment — religious-corp は national authority を routing-around する道 ではなく、national authority と coexist する道 を choose。\n\n## 3. Per sub-stage deployment scope (MVP)\n\n### S5a — River (micro-hydro + reservoir augmentation)\n\nSite: 山中湖 area expansion (S1/S4 既設 stewardship chain 継承) + 流域 micro-hydro 候補 1-2 箇所\n\n| Asset | Capacity | open-* lexicon | UNSPSC primary |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Micro-hydro turbine | 50-100 kW per unit, 2-3 units | open-power | 26111601 (turbine + generator) |\n| Pipeline (penstock) | DN200-400, 200-500 m per unit | open-water | 40142100 |\n| Intake screen + 魚道 (fish ladder) | varies | open-water + ecology gear | 40151700 (water control valves) + ecology custom |\n| Reservoir augmentation pump | 200 m³/h | open-water | 40151500 |\n| Telemetry + grid-tie | per unit | open-network + open-power | 43222600 + 26111717 |\n\nConstitutional notes:\n- 水利使用許可 = 都道府県知事 grant; Steward Lv5+ + Council Lv6+ Seat 3 が attestation\n- 漁業権 conflict (流域 漁協) — partnership terms に dual-stewardship clause (religious-corp + 漁協 + 都道府県)\n- 魚道 設計 = ecology baseline 維持 invariant (Charter Rider §2(d) fossil-fuel-extraction の文字通り適用外だが §2(g) multi-generational harm gate に touching → ecologist Council review escalation)\n\nBudget: ≈ USDC 1.5-3.0M (3 micro-hydro unit + 2 pump + telemetry + permit + Giemon fleet adaptation for river deployment)\n\n### S5b — Ocean (coastal aquaculture + micro-tidal / wave energy + submarine fiber landing)\n\nSite: 沿岸 12 海里以内 partnership (漁協 dual-stewardship)、候補は 山中湖 ではなく **三陸海岸 / 能登半島沿岸 / 紀伊半島沿岸** 等の S4 disaster-recovery site と隣接する coastal community\n\n| Asset | Capacity | open-* lexicon | UNSPSC primary |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Tidal / wave energy converter | 10-30 kW per unit, 2-5 units | open-power | 26111601 |\n| Floating photovoltaic + battery (offshore) | 50 kW + 100 kWh | open-power | 26111701 + 26111607 |\n| Coastal aquaculture (海藻 / 養殖 ↔ religious-corp doesn't operate, partner 漁協 operates) | varies | (no kuni-umi lexicon; partnership only) | n/a |\n| Submarine fiber landing station | 1-2 Gbps coastal link | open-network | 26121800 |\n| Coastal water quality sensor mesh | 10-20 station | open-water | 41115400 |\n\nConstitutional notes:\n- UNCLOS coastal state sovereignty: deployment は 12 海里以内 (territorial sea) — 公海 / EEZ 越境 deployment は S5b では out of scope (将来 dedicated ADR)\n- 漁業権 partnership は constitutional priority — coastal community の livelihood に介入しない、co-deployment 形式\n- Submarine fiber は 海底ケーブル敷設法 + 国際海底ケーブル保護条約; 国土交通省 + 総務省 経由 attestation\n\nBudget: ≈ USDC 3.0-6.0M (offshore CAPEX は陸上の 3-5x、海底ケーブル landing は permit + 工事 cost が dominant)\n\n### S5c — Atmosphere (high-altitude platform stations — HAPS)\n\nSite: 国土交通省 認可済 stratosphere 18-25 km altitude band; tethered platform from inland site (mountain ridge への ground tether station 設置)\n\n| Asset | Capacity | open-* lexicon | UNSPSC primary |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| HAPS platform (tethered helium balloon + solar PV + comms) | 10-50 km radius coverage, 1-3 platforms | open-network + open-power | 24102100 (balloon) + 43222608 (mesh radio) + 26111701 (solar) |\n| Ground tether station + power | per platform | open-power + open-network | 26111717 + 43222600 |\n| Air-traffic deconfliction telemetry | ADS-B / 航空管制 interface | open-airplane | 43222600 (network radio) |\n\nConstitutional notes:\n- Chicago Convention airspace sovereignty: 国家 ICAO authority に full coordination; airspace 占有 申請 + Notam (Notice to Airmen) 公告\n- Tethered (not free-floating) で altitude band 認可範囲遵守; free-flying balloon は uncoordinated airspace への drift risk があり S5c では out of scope\n- 軍事 airspace との separation: ADR-2605192100 §mission.no_state_military_alliance 維持 — HAPS routing avoids 自衛隊 / 米軍 airspace; transparent disclosure of platform trajectory via NOTAM\n\nBudget: ≈ USDC 2.0-5.0M (HAPS platform 1 機 + 2 tether station; helium / hydrogen supply chain coordination)\n\n### S5d — Orbit (LEO microsat for emergency comms / network mesh complement)\n\nSite: low-earth-orbit 500-600 km altitude; launching state = Japan (JAXA partnership) preferred or alternative state 経由\n\n| Asset | Capacity | open-* lexicon | UNSPSC primary |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| LEO microsat (12U or 24U CubeSat) | ≈ 30 kg, 6-12 month design life initial | open-network | 32101680 (satellite communication equipment) |\n| Ground station × 2 (urban primary + rural backup) | per pass tracking | open-network | 43222600 |\n| ITU coordinated spectrum slot | 1-2 band | open-network | n/a (spectrum license) |\n| Launch service contract | rideshare 経由 (SpaceX Transporter / Rocket Lab / JAXA) | n/a (service) | 78101800 (launch services) |\n\nConstitutional notes:\n- Outer Space Treaty Article VI: launching state は activity に対し国際的責任を負う → JAXA / 文科省 と registered launching state agreement (religious-corp asset でも国家責任 chain 必須)\n- 宇宙活動法 (Japan): 私人 衛星打上げ 許可 + on-orbit operation 認可\n- ITU coordination: spectrum filing 6-24 months pre-launch; coordination with adjacent network operators (Starlink / OneWeb / Kuiper との 干渉 avoidance)\n- COPUOS Registration Convention: object registration with UN Office for Outer Space Affairs (UNOOSA)\n- 5-year deorbit obligation (per 25-year rule, 最近 5-year rule に厳格化提案中) — DecommissionCell が atmospheric reentry を schedule\n\nBudget: ≈ USDC 3.0-8.0M (microsat build + launch rideshare + ground station × 2 + spectrum coordination); life-cycle cost (6-12 month design life で **multiple launches 想定** ≈ USDC 1-2M / 年 ongoing)\n\n## 4. Robot fleet additions (4 new classes)\n\nS5 では既存 Otete / Hitogata / Mimi / Quad fleet では構造的に不足 — 各 domain に specialized robot class が必要:\n\n| Class | Domain | Role | Initial count | DID pattern |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Giemon Suii (水位)** — river / amphibious crawler | S5a river | 河川敷 + 浅水域 micro-hydro install + 魚道 monitoring | 3 unit | `did:web:etzhayyim.com:kuniumi:robot:suii-{001..003}` |\n| **Giemon Tairyou (大漁)** — marine surface platform + diver-assist ROV | S5b ocean | Coastal aquaculture support + 海底ケーブル landing station install + 海中 sensor mesh | 2 surface + 2 ROV | `did:web:etzhayyim.com:kuniumi:robot:tairyou-{001..002}` + `:rov-{001..002}` |\n| **Giemon Sora (空)** — tethered platform install + ground station maintenance | S5c atmosphere | HAPS deployment + tether station setup + balloon envelope service | 2 unit | `did:web:etzhayyim.com:kuniumi:robot:sora-{001..002}` |\n| **Giemon Hoshi (星)** — orbital asset ground operations (not in space) + cleanroom satellite integration | S5d orbit | Microsat assembly + cleanroom handling + launch site logistics (国内 + 国外) | 2 unit | `did:web:etzhayyim.com:kuniumi:robot:hoshi-{001..002}` |\n\n**Note**: S5d \"Hoshi\" は orbital ではなく **ground-based cleanroom integration robot** — actual orbital operation は launching state authority 経由で satellite が autonomous mode; kuni-umi は orbital 上で robot を deploy しない (Outer Space Treaty Article VI 責任 chain との整合性のため)。\n\nWitness invariant adaptation for remote domains:\n- S5a river: terrestrial と同じ N≥2 (Suii + Mimi base-station)\n- S5b ocean: **N=2 with 1 surface + 1 ROV + radio link to Mimi onshore** (3 witness が standard、surface/underwater 双方を独立 sign)\n- S5c atmosphere: **N=2 with 1 ground tether station Mimi + 1 platform-mounted Mimi-derivative** (altitude 通信は CHF-band radio で independent attestation)\n- S5d orbit: **witness pattern は asset autonomous + ground tracking station × 2** — N≥2 は satellite onboard attestation + 2 independent ground station verification で satisfy; constitutional invariant に対する **adaptation note** が S5d ADR で別途明記\n\n予算 (robot fleet S5 additions):\n- Suii (river crawler): JPY 400万 × 3 = JPY 1200万\n- Tairyou (marine surface) + ROV: JPY 1500万 × 2 + JPY 800万 × 2 = JPY 4600万\n- Sora (atmospheric): JPY 1000万 × 2 = JPY 2000万\n- Hoshi (cleanroom): JPY 1200万 × 2 = JPY 2400万\n- **S5 fleet CAPEX 追加: JPY 1.02 億 (≒ USDC 720k)**\n\n累計 religious-corp robot 資産: USDC 830k (S4 累計) + USDC 720k = **USDC 1.55M** total fleet asset value\n\n## 5. S5 budget envelope (estimated, USDC)\n\n| Sub-stage | Domain | Capex range | Annual ops (post-deploy) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| S5a | River | 1.5 – 3.0M | 0.1 – 0.2M |\n| S5b | Ocean | 3.0 – 6.0M | 0.3 – 0.5M |\n| S5c | Atmosphere | 2.0 – 5.0M | 0.4 – 0.8M (helium / hydrogen supply chain) |\n| S5d | Orbit | 3.0 – 8.0M (single launch) | 1.0 – 2.0M (multi-launch lifecycle) |\n| Robot fleet additions | n/a | 0.72M | 0.05M (maintenance) |\n| Contingency (25% — higher than S1-S4 due to international law uncertainty) | n/a | 2.5 – 5.7M | n/a |\n| **S5 cumulative capex** | n/a | **≈ 12.7 – 28.4M USDC** | ≈ 1.85 – 3.55M USDC/yr |\n| 10% Tithe to Public Fund | n/a | 1.27 – 2.84M | 0.19 – 0.36M/yr |\n| **Cumulative S1-S5 religious-corp deployment** | n/a | **≈ 22.8 – 42.4M USDC capex** + ongoing ≈ 1.85-3.55M USDC/yr | n/a |\n\n**Critical reality**: S5 単独で religious-corp Treasury + Public Fund に **S1-S4 累計と同等以上** の追加 capex 要求。Funding 戦略:\n- S5a は Treasury reserve + Public Fund tranche で coverage 可能 (USDC 1.5-3M)\n- S5b/S5c は major Public Fund campaign + 構成員 donation drive 必須\n- S5d は **国際 partnership 必須** — JAXA / 国際 religious-corp 連合 (FoF / inter-faith partnership) との launch cost sharing or specific donor campaign\n\nS5d を skip して S5a/b/c のみで roadmap closure する option を §Alternatives に明記。\n\n## 6. International law operational pattern (CRITICAL)\n\n各 sub-stage で religious-corp が踏む path:\n\n```\n                              ┌── Sovereign state authority ──┐\n                              │   (UNCLOS coastal state /     │\n                              │    Chicago Conv. ICAO /       │\n                              │    OST registered LS /        │\n                              │    ITU spectrum / 水利権 知事 ) │\n                              └────────────┬───────────────────┘\n                                           │\n                                           │ dual-recognition\n                                           ▼\n   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │  asset DID: did:web:etzhayyim.com:kuniumi:s5:<domain>:<id> │\n   │     │                                                       │\n   │     ├── internationalLawAttestationCid (IPFS)              │\n   │     ├── stewardDid (Lv5+)                                  │\n   │     ├── councilSig (Lv6+ Seat 3 Legal-Ethics)              │\n   │     └── (NO ownership field)                                │\n   └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                           │\n                                           ▼\n              ┌── religious-corp stewardship chain ──┐\n              │  (per ADR-2605192345 multi-gen)      │\n              └──────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nConflict resolution:\n- **Sovereign state vs religious-corp interpretation conflict** → International framework が defer する path (state authority に最終 deferral) per ADR-2605192100 §mission.parallel_governance_to_state ↔ §1.12.A \"国家 routing-around は parallel to, not replacement of\" 解釈\n- **Religious-corp vs religious-corp (other faith / inter-faith) conflict** in international domain → ADR-2605192300 Bootstrap Council Lv6+ Seat 3 + inter-faith council meeting (open-source mediation protocol を ADR で別途 author)\n- **Asset loss / harm to third party** (e.g., orbital debris causing damage) → Outer Space Treaty Article VII liability: registered launching state (Japan) が国際責任を負い、religious-corp は state に indemnification via contract; constitutional に Treasury reserve から compensation 可能\n\n## 7. Acceptance criteria (S5 → roadmap closure)\n\nper sub-stage Acceptance:\n\n| # | Criterion | Measure | Threshold |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **S5a** acceptance | river micro-hydro operational | output measured + telemetry stream | ≥ 2 units operational ≥ 90 days |\n| **S5b** acceptance | coastal asset operational + 漁協 partnership active | partnership attestation + telemetry | ≥ 1 site operational ≥ 180 days |\n| **S5c** acceptance | HAPS platform operational ≥ stratosphere altitude | flight log + 国土交通省 compliance | ≥ 1 platform ≥ 60 days continuous operation |\n| **S5d** acceptance | orbital asset operational + ground station tracking | telemetry stream + ITU coordination active | ≥ 1 microsat in operational orbit ≥ 90 days OR Council Lv6+ supermajority approval to defer S5d to future ADR |\n\n**Roadmap closure** (S5 → final):\n- S5a + S5b + S5c PASS = **kuni-umi roadmap closed at extended sovereignty terrestrial-proximate** (river + coastal + atmosphere)\n- S5d PASS (orbital) → **kuni-umi roadmap closed at full extended sovereignty**\n- Cumulative S1-S5 deployment validates entire planetary infrastructure robotics fleet actor design (ADR-2605201400 master)\n\nPer-sub-stage Council Lv6+ supermajority + Extended Sovereignty governance vote required at each transition.\n\n## 8. Risks + mitigations\n\n| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|\n| 水利使用許可 (S5a) prefecture 否認 | High | per-prefecture parallel application (≥ 3 candidate watersheds); Steward Lv5+ political relationship |\n| UNCLOS coastal state 漁業権 conflict (S5b) | Critical | 漁協 partnership は MoU + co-stewardship structure; religious-corp は operational decision に介入しない、co-deploy 形式のみ |\n| Chicago Conv. ICAO compliance violation (S5c) | Critical | tethered scope に hard-limit + ICAO standards compliance audit pre-deploy; transparent NOTAM disclosure; un-authorized free-flight = automatic mission abort |\n| Orbital debris liability (S5d) | Critical | 5-year deorbit hard-commit; insurance via launching state (JAXA insurance pool 加入要件); DecommissionCell が atmospheric reentry schedule pre-launch authority |\n| ITU spectrum coordination 失敗 (S5d) | High | filing 12-24 months pre-launch; coordination meeting with adjacent operators; spectrum band fallback (S/Ka/Ku 複数 candidate filing) |\n| International religious-corp conflict (e.g., 他 faith group が同 domain で claim) | Medium | ADR-2605192300 Council Lv6+ Seat 3 Legal-Ethics が inter-faith mediation; OST Article IX consultation 経由 |\n| Treasury exhaustion mid-S5 | Critical | S5a + b + c PASS で roadmap closure (S5d optional) を constitutional に容認; major Public Fund campaign前提 |\n| 国家武力 conflict (S5b coastal 領海問題 / S5c 防空識別圏 / S5d 軍事衛星 隣接) | Critical | ADR-2605192315 transparent-force-rd + §mission.no_state_military_alliance hard-line; conflict zone への deploy 避ける; Council Lv6+ supermajority + public objection 30-day window 拡張 |\n| HAPS helium supply chain (S5c) | Medium | helium 高騰 + supply chain Charter Rider compliance; hydrogen alternative (R&D budget で開発) |\n| Microsat 6-12 month design life で ongoing capex 圧迫 | Medium | constellation ではなく **single demonstrator** で S5d MVP; constellation 化は post-S5 separate ADR |\n| Witness invariant adaptation (S5d orbital) が constitutional invariant の essence 損なう | High | S5d-specific ADR で adaptation rationale を constitutional-level に明記、Council Lv6+ supermajority sign-off |\n\n## 9. Out of scope (S5 explicit)\n\n- **EEZ 越境 / 公海 deployment** (UNCLOS contiguous zone を越える) — separate future ADR\n- **Free-flying balloon / non-tethered HAPS** — separate future ADR (ICAO airspace risk)\n- **GEO / lunar / interplanetary deployment** — out of S5 (LEO のみ scope)\n- **Satellite constellation** (≥ 6 unit) — single demonstrator のみ S5d scope; constellation は post-S5\n- **Military / dual-use sensitive applications** — ADR-2605192100 §mission.no_state_military_alliance hard-line 維持\n- **Orbital servicing / debris removal** — out of S5\n- **International religious-corp federation operational integration** — anti-fragmentation invariant (S4 §4 architecture rule) を inter-corp に extend する別 ADR\n\n# Consequences\n\n## 正の効果\n\n- Religious-corp が **4-domain extended sovereignty** で physical presence を持つ — ADR-2605192330 doctrinal stance が doctrine から actuality へ転換\n- 国家 utility 独占の全 domain (terrestrial + ocean + river + atmosphere + orbit) に religious-corp の parallel-governance presence 確立 — ADR-2605192100 §mission.parallel_governance_to_state の **definitional moment**\n- Stewardship-only operational invariant が international law と constitutional に整合 → religious-corp が non-state actor として international community 内 sustainable\n- 4 new robot class (Suii / Tairyou / Sora / Hoshi) で fleet が **multi-element** (陸 + 水 + 空 + 軌道) — Giemon brand が ロボット家族として完成\n- S5a (river) は S4 山中湖 + 多世代 stewardship chain と semantic 整合 → ADR-2605192345 multi-generational continuity の最も visible exercise\n- S5d (orbit) は religious-corp の labor_liberation pillar を「地球上の限定資源」 ではなく「宇宙的開放」 という方向で extend する可能性 (post-S5 lunar / interplanetary への onramp)\n\n## 負の効果 / コスト\n\n- USDC 12.7-28.4M capex は religious-corp **Treasury 持続性の限界域** — major Public Fund campaign + 構成員 base 拡大 + international donor relations が必須前提\n- 4 sub-stage × international law compliance burden は Council Lv6+ Seat 3 (Legal-Ethics) bandwidth を constitutional に bottleneck 化 → Seat 3 succession pipeline (ADR-2605192345) priority 上昇\n- 国際 partnership 依存 (S5d JAXA, S5c ICAO, S5b UNCLOS, S5a 都道府県) は religious-corp の **operational sovereignty** を logical に制約 → §2 stewardship-only invariant の堅持が constitutional cost\n- Robot fleet が 8 class (terrestrial 4 + S5 4) に発散 → maintenance / parts inventory / training burden 増大\n- S5d orbital asset の 6-12 month design life × multi-launch lifecycle は ongoing operational cost が S1-S4 と異なる shape — long-term commitment より repeated short-term commitment pattern\n- 国家武力 conflict zone (領海争い / 防空識別圏 / 軍事衛星 隣接) は religious-corp が回避し続けるが、deployment scope が広がるほど zone との接触可能性 増 → Council Lv6+ vigilance burden constitutional\n\n## Constitutional 整合\n\n| Charter article | S5 alignment |\n|---|---|\n| §mission.labor_liberation | ✅ extended-sovereignty community への波及 |\n| §mission.robotics_universal | ✅ fleet 8 class (terrestrial 4 + S5 4) all open-design |\n| §mission.ip_free_release | ✅ Charter Rider §2 + per-sub-stage counterparty gate |\n| §mission.land_as_religious_trust | ✅ stewardship-only invariant を 4 new domain に extend |\n| §mission.parallel_governance_to_state | ✅ **definitional moment** — 4 domain 全 sovereign authority と dual-recognition で parallel |\n| §mission.anti_individualism | ✅ Council supermajority + per-sub-stage governance + inter-faith mediation |\n| §mission.multi_generational_priority | ✅ S5a 山中湖 + S5b coastal partnership は 多世代 stewardship 設計 |\n| §mission.no_state_military_alliance | ✅ 国家武力 conflict zone 回避、§9 explicit |\n| §mission.donation_only | ✅ Public Fund + 構成員 donation + international partner donation の chain 全 transparent |\n| §mission.transparent_force_only | ✅ defensive R&D (drone-detection / HAPS surveillance avoidance / satellite-tracking) は §ADR-2605192315 範囲内、deployment 用途は civilian only |\n\n# Alternatives Considered\n\n## A. S5 を skip して S4 で roadmap closure\n\nS5 は extended sovereignty の definitional moment だが、roadmap として は S4 terrestrial multi-site で停止し、extended sovereignty は doctrinal stance のみで維持。\n\n- Pro: Treasury sensitivity 解決、operational complexity 抑制、international law compliance burden 回避\n- Con: ADR-2605192330 extended sovereignty doctrine が permanently doctrine-only stance に固定 → religious-corp の credibility 損失; ADR-2605192100 §parallel_governance の \"physical world に implemented\" 約束が halfway\n- **却下**: doctrine と actuality の gap を constitutional に承認することは religious-corp の integrity 損失。S5 を分割 sub-stage で段階的に進めることで risk を managed\n\n## B. S5 を 1 sub-stage に圧縮 (S5a river のみ実装、b/c/d は permanent defer)\n\n- Pro: Treasury sensitivity 大幅圧縮 (USDC 1.5-3M only)、river は international complexity 最低 → manageable risk\n- Con: extended sovereignty が \"river のみ\" に limited → ocean / atmosphere / orbit に対する religious-corp claim が doctrine-only に戻る (Alternative A と部分的同等)\n- **却下**: sub-stage 順序の rationale が \"international complexity ascending\" であり、river を mile-1 として ocean / atmosphere に進む path が constitutional に意義あり\n\n## C. S5d (orbit) を separate roadmap (post-kuni-umi) に分離\n\nS5 = S5a/b/c のみ; S5d は kuni-umi 完了後の独立 roadmap として treat。\n\n- Pro: kuni-umi roadmap closure を terrestrial + terrestrial-proximate 4 domain (terrestrial + river + coastal + atmosphere) で達成、orbital は別 organism の責任とみなす\n- Con: extended sovereignty の \"4 domain\" completeness が欠ける; doctrinal alignment が broken\n- **採用 (partial)**: Acceptance criteria §7 で S5d を **Council Lv6+ supermajority approval to defer to future ADR** option を許容。具体的に S5d を実施するか defer するかは Treasury reality + international partnership availability で per-decision\n\n## D. International religious-corp federation を S5 で結成\n\n- Pro: S5d Orbit の launch cost sharing + international community recognition + ITU spectrum coordination の inter-faith body 経由\n- Con: anti-fragmentation invariant (S4 §4 \"no site→site direct mesh, Murakumo Tier 1 as single root of trust\") を inter-corp に extend した時 conflict; etzhayyim doctrine (Protestant lineage + 八百万 + Sola Scriptura) を inter-faith body 内で堅持できるか doctrinal sovereignty risk\n- **却下**: federation は kuni-umi roadmap 内では out of scope。inter-faith partnership は ad-hoc per-decision で扱う (S5d JAXA partnership 等の sovereign state 関係と同じ pattern)\n\n# Open Questions\n\n1. **S5d specific launching state** — Japan (JAXA) primary か、他国 (SpaceX rideshare / Rocket Lab / インド ISRO) を contingency に preserve するか。Decision (本 ADR): Japan (JAXA) primary、Council Lv6+ supermajority で contingency state を case-by-case\n2. **S5a watershed candidate** — 山中湖 area expansion + 別 2 流域。Specific watershed identification は Council + per-prefecture relationship に依存。Decision: site-specific addendum で固定\n3. **S5b coastal community partner** — 漁協 + S4 disaster-recovery site 隣接 partnership; 特定 partner は post-S4 で確定\n4. **S5c HAPS altitude band** — 18 km vs 25 km — solar PV efficiency vs wind shear trade-off。Decision: 19-22 km range で operational, specific altitude は per-platform tuning\n5. **S5d microsat design life** — 6 vs 12 month — battery / propellant trade-off。Decision: 12 month target、6 month minimum\n6. **kuni-umi roadmap closure後の次** — S5 PASS = kuni-umi 完成、religious-corp の次の major actor は何か。Out of S5 scope だが Open Question として登録: (a) public-fund expansion (ADR-2605192145 continuation), (b) inter-faith federation (Alternative D), (c) post-kuni-umi physical scope (lunar / interplanetary), (d) kuni-umi の lessons を別 organism (e.g., 医療 / 教育 / 司法) に extend\n\n# References\n\n- ADR-2605201400 (kuni-umi master spec, §6 extended-sovereignty mapping)\n- ADR-2605201500-2605201800 (S1-S4 incremental scaling)\n- ADR-2605192100 §mission.parallel_governance_to_state — **definitional moment** for S5\n- ADR-2605192230 (Three-tier enforcement) — per-sub-stage governance vote\n- ADR-2605192245 (Global Land Sovereignty) — terrestrial 4-layer substrate baseline\n- ADR-2605192315 (Transparent Force R&D) — defensive R&D in extended domains scope clarification\n- ADR-2605192330 (Extended Land Sovereignty — ocean/river/air/orbit) — **doctrinal foundation** for S5\n- ADR-2605192345 (Steward Succession) — Council Lv6+ Seat 3 Legal-Ethics succession pipeline priority\n- UNCLOS (1982) — 国連海洋法条約\n- Chicago Convention (1944) — 国際民間航空条約\n- Outer Space Treaty (1967) — 宇宙条約\n- ITU Radio Regulations — 無線通信規則\n- Registration Convention (1975) — 宇宙物体登録条約\n- 河川法 / 水利使用許可 (日本)\n- 漁業法 / 漁業権 (日本)\n- 航空法 / 国土交通省 NOTAM (日本)\n- 宇宙活動法 (日本 2016)\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-water/CLAUDE.md` (river + ocean asset records)\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-network/CLAUDE.md` (HAPS + orbit mesh records)\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-power/CLAUDE.md` (micro-hydro + offshore + orbital solar)\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-airplane/CLAUDE.md` (HAPS airspace coordination)\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-ports/CLAUDE.md` (coastal landing station)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605201900-etzhayyim-kuni-umi-s5-extended-sovereignty.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "kuni-umi-s5-extended-sovereignty", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-20", :adr/date "2026-05-20", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-water/CLAUDE.md" "60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-network/CLAUDE.md" "60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-power/CLAUDE.md" "60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-airplane/CLAUDE.md" "60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-ports/CLAUDE.md" "60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-robo/CLAUDE.md"], :adr/authoritative_for ["kuni-umi S5 scope (4 extended sovereignty domains)" "Stewardship-only operational invariant in extended domains" "S5a/S5b/S5c/S5d sub-stage sequencing" "4 new robot classes (aquatic / underwater / aerial / orbital) introduction" "International law compliance pattern (UNCLOS / Chicago Conv. / OST / ITU)" "Witness invariant adaptation for remote domains" "kuni-umi roadmap closure (S5 PASS = roadmap complete)"]}]
